        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(channels): share durable ingress monitor",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nLINE, Mattermost, Microsoft Teams, Nextcloud Talk, SMS, and Zalo each carried local copies of durable ingress admission, drain scheduling, claim lifecycle, retention, and shutdown coordination. Those copies could drift in subtle replay and restart behavior even though they enforce the same core invariant.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMoves the shared ingress mechanics into `createChannelIngressMonitor` while keeping each plugin's event identity, payload codec, lane policy, transport acknowledgement, failure classification, retention limits, and channel-owned shutdown contracts local. The shared helper gains only the generic seams required by the six existing behaviors, including atomic batch admission, append-only late admission, detached pump execution, and channel-owned delivery-idle policy.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intentional user-visible behavior or configuration change. Durable webhook replay and shutdown behavior now use one implementation across these plugins, with channel-specific delivery semantics preserved.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 120 focused tests pass across all six plugins and `src/channels/message/ingress-monitor.test.ts` after rebasing onto current `main`.\n- Core, core-test, extension, and extension-test `tsgo` lanes pass.\n- Production/full-tree/script unused-export scans and production/full-tree unused-file scans report zero entries.\n- Targeted `oxlint`, touched-file `oxfmt`, plugin SDK API baseline, and `git diff --check` pass.\n- Mandatory branch autoreview completed with no accepted or actionable findings.\n",
